# This represents a simple lambda function.
# A function is formed using arguments and body
# ________
# |      |----> Lambda Function
# (\x. x) a
#   |  |  |
#   |  |  +--> variable (argument), the function is being applied to
#   |  +-----> body of the function
#   +--------> parameter of the funcition
#
# The whole pattern is:
# (λx. M) N
# This is called a beta-redex: a lambda function applied to an argument.
#
# Beta-reduction applies the function:
# (λx. M) N  -> β  M[x := N]
#                         |-- substitute `N` for `x` in the body `M`
#
# For this example:
#   M = x
#   N = a
#
# Substitute a for x in the body:
#   M[x := N] = x[x := a] = a
#
# Therefore:
#   (λx. x) a  -> β  a
# This step is called beta-reduction.
#
# So, basically what we do is just replace the free occurance of parameter
# inside the body of the function with the `term` function is being applied to.
#
# > term: any valid expression
#
# There, `(\x. x)` takes anything and returns it, so applying it to `a` will return `a`

(λx. x)a
